This license covers the Crumbs HUD software: the server (crumbs_hud.py),
the map engine (crumbs_core.py), the editor page (editor.html), and the
bundled starter art and template maps. Your maps and your imported art
are yours — this license governs the software and the art packs it ships.

1. EDITIONS

   FREE — the core editor. Personal and non-commercial use. You may run
   it on as many of your own devices as you like. You may not sell,
   rent, or redistribute the software itself.

   CREATOR — [PRICE], one-time. Everything in Free, plus: the curated
   starter art packs, the advanced toolset (sprite-sheet importer,
   generation presets, mission workshop), and commercial use of maps and
   games you make with it, up to $[REVENUE CAP] gross revenue per year
   across all your projects combined.

   PRO — [PRICE], one-time. Everything in Creator, plus: full commercial
   use with no revenue cap, including redistribution of exported bundles
   (PNG maps, map bundles, exported data files) as part of your own
   products, and priority support.

2. WHAT "COMMERCIAL USE OF MAPS YOU MAKE" MEANS

   Your maps are your work. On Creator and Pro you may sell games built
   on maps you made, show them in monetized videos, and use them in
   client work. On Free you may not — maps stay personal.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO (all editions)

   - Resell, sublicense, or redistribute the Crumbs HUD software itself.
   - Remove or alter the splash-screen credit.
   - Use the software to make anything illegal. (Had to say it.)

4. ART YOU DIDN'T MAKE

   Tile art has its own licenses, which travel with the art, not with
   this license. See COMMERCIAL_TERMS.md: the starter pack is original
   art by Lloyd; the Utumno sheet is CC0 public domain; art you import
   is your responsibility; the Minecraft InvSprite pack is personal-use
   only and is never licensed for redistribution.

5. NO WARRANTY

   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. It
   is built and maintained by one person; support is best-effort (see
